<h1>Fit Sphere</h1>
<hr align="left" width="100.526%" size="5" class="whs3">
<p><span lang="EN-GB">This command is accessible from</span> <span class="Path" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Measure &gt; Geometry &gt; Sphere</b></span> <span lang="EN-GB">or by pressing</span> <b><span class="Shortcut" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Alt + 4</b></span></b><span lang="EN-GB">.</span></p>
<p class="Description"><span class="Command" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Description:</b></span> <span class="Command">Fit Sphere</span> <span lang="EN-GB">command fits a datum sphere to the visible selection, which may include scan data, meshes, point clouds, datum points and polylines. This command is grayed if there is no selection or all selections are hidden.</span></p>
<p class="Note" id="P1"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Note</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: If needed to fit sphere to existing datums, you should use datum points only. Including other datums in the selection will lead to incorrect results.</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><span lang="EN-GB">After the sphere is fitted the following dialog will appear in the Tool pane:</span></p>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;"><img src="../Measure/images/fit_sphere.gif" width="220px" height="424px" border="0" class="img_whs4" alt=""></p>
<p class="parameterstitle">Deviation</p>
<ul>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Max/Min value</b></span>: Maximum deviations from the outer and inner sides of the fitted sphere.</p>
</li>
<li class="kadov-p-Cbullet">
<p class="bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Fixed radius</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: Enter a predefined radius for the sphere to be detected.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="Normal" style="text-align:justify;">The dialog includes the following statistics:</p>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Centre</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>X</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Y</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">,</span> <span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Z</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">:</span> <span lang="EN-GB">&#160;co-ordinates of the centre of the fitted sphere.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Statistics</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Radius</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: the radius calculated from the selected data.</span></p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span lang="EN-GB" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>RMS error</b></span><span lang="EN-GB">: Root Mean Square distance from the point to the selected points.</span></p>
</li>
</ul>
<p class="parameterstitle"><span lang="EN-GB">Buttons</span></p>
<ul class="whs5">
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Recalculate</b></span>: fits a sphere again according to the current deviations.</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Create sphere</b></span>: creates a datum sphere entity from the fit data.</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Plot</b></span>: calls the error distribution plot dialog.</p>
</li>
<li style="text-align:justify;" class="kadov-p-CBullet">
<p class="Bullet"><span class="Button" style="font-weight:bold;"><b>Close</b></span>: exits this mode.</p>
</li>
</ul>
<p>After the sphere is fitted, the error map is displayed.</p>
